     LIME_SSTX_P: +0.000 to +5.000 V. LIME_SSTX_P: J_LIME pin 9, the LimeSDR Mini 2.4's USB 3 receive pair through the receptacle. The LimeSDR in its bay has no supply but this receptacle's VBUS, +5V_LIME (declared 5.0 V), so its pins stay within 0 V and that supply (the premise rule V-1 applies to every active part, here to the module behind the connector; its USB 3.0 controller is an FTDI FT601, whose own sheet is not held). Operating case: the LimeSDR enumerated at USB 3 speed; round 5 of record l6r2
     LIME_SSTX_N: +0.000 to +5.000 V. LIME_SSTX_N: J_LIME pin 8, the LimeSDR Mini 2.4's USB 3 receive pair through the receptacle. The LimeSDR in its bay has no supply but this receptacle's VBUS, +5V_LIME (declared 5.0 V), so its pins stay within 0 V and that supply (the premise rule V-1 applies to every active part, here to the module behind the connector; its USB 3.0 controller is an FTDI FT601, whose own sheet is not held). Operating case: the LimeSDR enumerated at USB 3 speed; round 5 of record l6r2
     W1A_CARD: -10.620 to +10.620 V. the slot 1 card's antenna lead (J_W1A), chain A: the AsiaRF AW7915-AED's highest conducted output is 23 dBm +/- 1.5 dB (11b, datasheet V1.0 p.3), 24.5 dBm, which is 5.31 V peak into 50 Ohm and 10.62 V with the lead fully reflecting (an open or shorted antenna, the case board B's LORA_ANT declares). DC: none (an antenna lead, DC blocked on the switch side). Operating case: transmit at full power into any load; round 5 of record l6r2
